---
/** The four application patterns the design document lists in §3.4: a remote smart contract call (§3.4.1), escrow then mint then burn (§3.4.2), an N-ledger atomic swap by two-phase commit (§3.4.3), and native Hiero asset management (§3.4.4). General page section 11; the rows of src/data/patterns.json name the same four. */
import Figure from '@kse/components/Figure.astro';
import { design } from '../../../lib/sources';
---
<Figure
  lead="Four things people build on one message primitive."
  caption="A call to a contract on another ledger, with the result coming back later. Assets locked on one ledger and minted on another, released if the mint fails. Several ledgers changing state together or not at all. And Hiero tokens moving between Hiero networks with no contract proxies in between. All four are just messages with replies."
  source={[{ label: 'design §3.4.1', href: design('341-remote-smart-contract-call') }, { label: 'design §3.4.2', href: design('342-escrow-mint-then-burn') }, { label: 'design §3.4.3', href: design('343-n-ledger-atomic-swap-2pc') }, { label: 'design §3.4.4', href: design('344-native-hiero-asset-management') }]}
  kind="plain"
  minWidth={760}
>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 358" role="img" aria-label="Four panels. Remote call: an application on Ledger A calls a proxy, the call travels to a proxy on Ledger B which invokes the target contract, and the result travels back. Escrow, mint, burn: assets locked on A, minted on B, then burned on A, or released on A if the mint fails. Atomic swap: three ledgers each answer ready, then all commit, or one fails and all roll back. Native Hiero assets: a token moves from one Hiero network to another through the messaging layer with no proxies.">
    <!-- panel 1: remote call -->
    <rect x="10" y="12" width="158" height="318" rx="10" class="d-surface" />
    <text x="89" y="36" class="t b center">Remote call</text>
    <rect x="22" y="52" width="134" height="40" rx="8" class="d-a" />
    <text x="89" y="70" class="t center">application on A</text>
    <text x="89" y="85" class="t small center">calls a proxy</text>
    <line x1="89" y1="92" x2="89" y2="134" class="line c" />
    <text x="100" y="116" class="t small">a message</text>
    <rect x="22" y="134" width="134" height="40" rx="8" class="d-b" />
    <text x="89" y="152" class="t center">proxy on B</text>
    <text x="89" y="167" class="t small center">invokes the target</text>
    <rect x="22" y="192" width="134" height="40" rx="8" class="d-b" />
    <text x="89" y="210" class="t center">target contract</text>
    <text x="89" y="225" class="t small center">does the work</text>
    <line x1="56" y1="232" x2="56" y2="270" class="line b dash" />
    <text x="64" y="256" class="t small">the result, later</text>
    <text x="89" y="304" class="t small center muted">written for</text>
    <text x="89" y="319" class="t small center muted">asynchronous answers</text>

    <!-- panel 2: escrow, mint, burn -->
    <rect x="178" y="12" width="190" height="318" rx="10" class="d-surface" />
    <text x="273" y="36" class="t b center">Escrow, mint, burn</text>
    <rect x="190" y="52" width="166" height="40" rx="8" class="d-a" />
    <text x="273" y="70" class="t center">1 lock on A</text>
    <text x="273" y="85" class="t small center">assets held in escrow</text>
    <line x1="273" y1="92" x2="273" y2="134" class="line c" />
    <rect x="190" y="134" width="166" height="40" rx="8" class="d-b" />
    <text x="273" y="152" class="t center">2 mint on B</text>
    <text x="273" y="167" class="t small center">matching assets issued</text>
    <line x1="230" y1="174" x2="230" y2="212" class="line ok" />
    <line x1="316" y1="174" x2="316" y2="212" class="line bad dash" />
    <rect x="190" y="212" width="80" height="40" rx="8" class="d-ok" />
    <text x="230" y="230" class="t small center">3 burn on A</text>
    <text x="230" y="244" class="t small center">if it worked</text>
    <rect x="276" y="212" width="80" height="40" rx="8" class="d-bad" />
    <text x="316" y="230" class="t small center">release</text>
    <text x="316" y="244" class="t small center">if it failed</text>
    <text x="273" y="304" class="t small center muted">needs a common</text>
    <text x="273" y="319" class="t small center muted">asset standard</text>

    <!-- panel 3: atomic swap -->
    <rect x="378" y="12" width="192" height="318" rx="10" class="d-surface" />
    <text x="474" y="36" class="t b center">Atomic swap, N ledgers</text>
    <text x="474" y="60" class="t small center">1 each gets ready, and says so</text>
    <rect x="390" y="70" width="52" height="34" rx="8" class="d-a" /><text x="416" y="92" class="t center">A</text>
    <rect x="448" y="70" width="52" height="34" rx="8" class="d-b" /><text x="474" y="92" class="t center">B</text>
    <rect x="506" y="70" width="52" height="34" rx="8" class="d-c" /><text x="532" y="92" class="t center">C</text>
    <line x1="416" y1="104" x2="416" y2="136" class="line a" />
    <line x1="474" y1="104" x2="474" y2="136" class="line b" />
    <line x1="532" y1="104" x2="532" y2="136" class="line c" />
    <rect x="390" y="142" width="168" height="40" rx="8" class="d-ok" />
    <text x="474" y="160" class="t center">all ready → all commit</text>
    <text x="474" y="175" class="t small center">the changes land together</text>
    <rect x="390" y="194" width="168" height="40" rx="8" class="d-bad" />
    <text x="474" y="212" class="t center">one fails → all roll back</text>
    <text x="474" y="227" class="t small center">nothing lands anywhere</text>
    <text x="474" y="262" class="t small center">two-phase commit, carried</text>
    <text x="474" y="277" class="t small center">as ordinary messages</text>
    <text x="474" y="304" class="t small center muted">every ledger must</text>
    <text x="474" y="319" class="t small center muted">speak the protocol</text>

    <!-- panel 4: native Hiero assets -->
    <rect x="580" y="12" width="170" height="318" rx="10" class="d-surface" />
    <text x="665" y="36" class="t b center">Native Hiero assets</text>
    <rect x="592" y="52" width="146" height="56" rx="8" class="d-a" />
    <text x="665" y="74" class="t center">Hiero network 1</text>
    <text x="665" y="92" class="t small center">a token, fungible or not</text>
    <line x1="632" y1="108" x2="632" y2="176" class="line a" />
    <text x="642" y="140" class="t small">moves by the</text>
    <text x="642" y="154" class="t small">messaging layer</text>
    <rect x="592" y="176" width="146" height="56" rx="8" class="d-a" />
    <text x="665" y="198" class="t center">Hiero network 2</text>
    <text x="665" y="216" class="t small center">the same token, here</text>
    <text x="665" y="262" class="t small center">no contract proxies</text>
    <text x="665" y="304" class="t small center muted">CLPR-native handling</text>

    <text x="380" y="350" class="t take center">Four patterns, one primitive: a data message that always gets exactly one reply.</text>
  </svg>
</Figure>
